  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Remove from Levels**: Find three adjacent tiles in any level that form a valid triplet. Remove them and add them to the left of the Common Row.\n2. **Cut Generals**: When a level has only 1 tile left, use it with the two rightmost tiles from the Common Row to form a valid triplet. If valid, remove all three and flip the next General face-up.\n3. **Critical Move**: Exactly ONCE in the game, you must use a single-tile level to cut TWO generals simultaneously (using the rightmost Common Row tile and the two rightmost Generals).\n4. **Winning**: Win by clearing all levels and cutting all six generals.\n5. **Losing**: Lose if the Common Row is empty and no valid triplet can be removed from any level.',
    Player: '1. **Remove from Levels**: Find three adjacent tiles in any level that form a valid triplet. Remove them and add them to the left of the Common Row.\n2. **Cut Generals**: When a level has only 1 tile left, use it with the two rightmost tiles from the Common Row to form a valid triplet. If valid, remove all three and flip the next General face-up.\n3. **Critical Move**: Exactly ONCE in the game, you must use a single-tile level to cut TWO generals simultaneously (using the rightmost Common Row tile and the two rightmost Generals).\n4. **Winning**: Win by clearing all levels and cutting all six generals.\n5. **Losing**: Lose if the Common Row is empty and no valid triplet can be removed from any level.',
    objective: 'Pass all five levels and cut all six generals by removing valid triplets of tiles.',
    gameplay: '1. **Remove from Levels**: Find three adjacent tiles in any level that form a valid triplet. Remove them and add them to the left of the Common Row.\n2. **Cut Generals**: When a level has only 1 tile left, use it with the two rightmost tiles from the Common Row to form a valid triplet. If valid, remove all three and flip the next General face-up.\n3. **Critical Move**: Exactly ONCE in the game, you must use a single-tile level to cut TWO generals simultaneously (using the rightmost Common Row tile and the two rightmost Generals).\n4. **Winning**: Win by clearing all levels and cutting all six generals.\n5. **Losing**: Lose if the Common Row is empty and no valid triplet can be removed from any level.',
