      'Rule example: Pass all five levels and cut all six generals by removing valid triplets of tiles.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Remove from Levels**: Find three adjacent tiles in any level that form a valid triplet. Remove them and add them to the left of the Common Row.\n2. **Cut Generals**: When a level has only 1 tile left, use it with the two rightmost tiles from the Common Row to form a valid triplet. If valid, remove all three and flip the next General face-up.\n3. **Critical Move**: Exactly ONCE in the game, you must use a single-tile level to cut TWO generals simultaneously (using the rightmost Common Row tile and the two rightmost Generals).\n4. **Winning**: Win by clearing all levels and cutting all six generals.\n5. **Losing**: Lose if the Common Row is empty and no valid triplet can be removed from any level.',
      'Scoring example: No point score. Win by passing all five levels and cutting all six generals; lose if the common row is empty and no valid triplet can be removed. Pass all five levels and cut all six generals. The game is lost if the common row is empty and there is no valid triplet of adjacent tiles in any remaining level..',
